From: Keel maintainers <maintainers@keel.dev>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] preserve literal argv through POSIX sandbox wrapping

Local incremental patch record against Keel's reviewed
@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime v0.0.59 postimage
(upstream 3f4233f173227ca2e9dfde8c4985bc31811a64fc).

The reviewed postimage is carried in these vendored paths:

- src/sandbox/posix-shell-quote.ts
- src/sandbox/macos-sandbox-utils.ts
- src/sandbox/linux-sandbox-utils.ts
- test/sandbox/posix-shell-quote.test.ts

Root cause:

shell-quote chooses double quotes for an already-rendered command string that
contains whitespace and single quotes, then emits a defensive backslash before
`!`. POSIX shells retain that backslash inside double quotes. A direct-argv
`process.run` request therefore reached the contained child with an extra byte,
despite the Warden retaining and auditing the exact original argv.

Contract anchors required by Keel's vendor verifier:

- quotePosixShellArgs
- values containing `!` use lossless single-quote rendering
- all other values retain upstream shell-quote rendering
- macOS and Linux outer sandbox command layers use the lossless helper
- Linux nested user-command and seccomp layers use the lossless helper
- no shell composition, environment, cwd, stdin, background, or retry authority
  is added to process.run

Evidence:

- deterministic two-layer shell round trip for `!`, `!==`, existing backslash
  plus `!`, embedded single quote plus `!`, and an empty argument;
- real macOS Seatbelt argv round trip through the vendored launch-authority path;
- the existing process.run injection property and all neighboring shell-looking
  literal arguments remain data and create no sibling effect.

Security and compatibility:

The patch restores the requested byte vector. Validation, policy, sandbox
profile, audit intent/outcome, review binding, no-retry behavior, TLS and
credential handling are unchanged. Rendering is unchanged when an argument
contains no exclamation mark. The patch is minimal and upstreamable; recorded
2026-08-12 and not yet submitted upstream.
